{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017z2R6QLbQJkNih35KnofPr","type":"tool_result","content":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-challenger-9k5lbjt2\ntotal 16\ndrwx------@     4 brenn  staff      128 Oct 20 18:24 .\ndrwx------@ 49975 brenn  staff  1599200 Oct 20 18:24 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x@    14 brenn  staff      448 Oct  2 12:21 agent\n-rw-r--r--@     1 brenn  staff     5016 Oct 20 18:24 sheet.md\n# Independent coverage discovery: R04 — Retrieval-corpus integrity\n\nEstablish your own findings from the code before comparing with any earlier\nreview. You are not told the earlier rating, answers, citations or exceptions.\n**Requirement:** The retrieval corpus is the set of documents the agent searches for context. Its index stores those documents, or smaller passages called chunks, in a search engine or vector database. Limit which identities and sources can add or change content there. For each chunk, keep its source, when it was added, its trust level, and its access permissions. Enforce the requesting tenant's access when searching. Test an unapproved attempt to add content and a search across tenants. Also test quarantining, expiring, and revoking access to seeded test documents. Confirm the affected chunks disappear from search results and caches within a stated time. See the [R04 recipe](CHECKLIST-VERIFICATION.md#r--run-time).\n**N/A condition:** Only when the agent has no retrieval corpus or search index.\n\nInventory all relevant paths/fields, including indirect paths, helpers and both directions of\nhandoffs. For each check, record coverage rows (subject, status enforced/missing/\nunclear/not_applicable, evidence, exact quote, note), deviations (required-control\nomissions; empty only if none), and concrete falsification attempts (category,\ninput, trace, outcome blocked/accepted/unclear/not_applicable, evidence, quote).\nSmall or residual omissions are still omissions. A missing row or unresolved\ncoverage cannot support holds. Do not run repository code; derive counterexamples\nby tracing it. A bounded_after budget claim needs a finite overshoot bound, not\njust a shared counter. Exemptions need quoted scope evidence.\n\nSet applicability absent/present/unclear, with top-level evidence, quote and a\nsearch explanation. Absent must satisfy the exact N/A condition. When present,\nverdict is failed if any required check fails, unclear if any is unresolved,\notherwise upheld. Copy broken words from the requirement into violates.\n\n\n## R04.1\n\n**Check:** Only named identities and sources can add or change index content, and the ingestion path checks the writer.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Find index write paths (`upsert`, `add_documents`, `index`, ingestion jobs). 2) Check each verifies the writer identity or source against a named list. 3) Answer no if any write path, including the agent's own tools or an admin endpoint, accepts writes without that check.\n\n**Coverage policy:** {}\n\n**Candidate sites (trace aliases and missed paths manually):** []\n\n## R04.2\n\n**Check:** Each stored chunk has metadata for source, time added, trust level, and access permissions.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Find chunk write code and metadata fields. 2) Check source, time added, trust level, and access permissions are stored on every chunk. 3) Answer no if any field is missing, or set only on some ingestion paths.\n\n**Coverage policy:** {}\n\n**Candidate sites (trace aliases and missed paths manually):** []\n\n## R04.3\n\n**Check:** Search applies the requesting tenant's access filter at query time, in the store or retrieval code, not after the model answers.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Find search calls (`similarity_search`, `query`, `search`, `filter=`, `where=`). 2) Check a tenant or access filter is applied in the store query, from the caller's identity. 3) Answer no if filtering happens after retrieval or in the prompt, the filter is optional, or the tenant comes from a model-supplied argument.\n\n**Coverage policy:** {}\n\n**Candidate sites (trace aliases and missed paths manually):** []\n\n## R04.4\n\n**Check:** Code can quarantine, expire, and revoke chunks, and it also clears or invalidates search caches.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Find quarantine, expiry, and revoke code (`delete`, `quarantine`, `ttl`, `expires_at`). 2) Check search excludes those chunks and caches are cleared. 3) Answer no if any of the three operations is missing, or caches (query cache, embedding cache) are not invalidated.\n\n**Coverage policy:** {}\n\n**Candidate sites (trace aliases and missed paths manually):** []\n\n## Your answer\n\nWrite this JSON to R04.verdict.json in this folder (or put it in verdicts.json under \"R04\"):\n```json\n{\"verdict\": \"upheld | failed | unclear\",\n \"checks\": [{\"id\": \"R04.1\", \"result\": \"holds | fails | unclear\", \"evidence\": \"path:line\", \"quote\": \"exact code\", \"note\": \"why\", \"coverage\": [], \"deviations\": [], \"attempts\": []}],\n \"applicability\": \"absent | present | unclear\", \"evidence\": \"path:line\", \"quote\": \"exact code\",\n \"note\": \"one sentence\"}\n```\nVerdict is **failed** if any check fails, **unclear** if none fails but any is unclear, otherwise **upheld**. A failed check needs the quoted line that makes it false: `evidence` is path:line, and `quote` is the exact text of that line. To cite two places, list both refs in `evidence` (`a.py:12, b.yaml:40`) and put each line's text on its own line in `quote`. If the check fails, add `\"violates\": [\"words copied exactly from the requirement\"]`.\nagent\nagent/infra\nagent/infra/terraform\nagent/infra/terraform/main.tf\nagent/infra/terraform/github.tf\nagent/infra/terraform/iam.tf\nagent/test\nagent/test/controls.test.ts\nagent/test/budget.test.ts\nagent/config\nagent/config/tools.allowlist.yaml\nagent/config/policy.yaml\nagent/config/budgets.yaml\nagent/Dockerfile\nagent/k8s\nagent/k8s/deployment.yaml\nagent/release\nagent/release/manife